t contamination of its solar arrays ended operations.",[434,438,441,445,448],{"met":63,"label":435,"note":436,"type":437},"LAUNCH","Proton-K from Baikonur 1973-01-08.","nominal",{"met":68,"label":439,"note":440,"type":437},"TLI","Trans-lunar injection on the Blok-D upper stage.",{"met":73,"label":442,"note":443,"type":444},"TCM","Mid-course correction during cruise.","info",{"met":12,"label":446,"note":447,"type":437},"LANDING","Soft landing in Le Monnier crater 1973-01-15. Lunokhod 2 rolled off ramps a few hours later.",{"met":82,"label":449,"note":450,"type":437},"ROVER ACTIVE","Five-person ground crew in Crimea began driving operations. Total traverse: ~39 km.","/orrery/images/missions/luna21/06.webp"],"uses":{"params":["id"]}}]}
